Assignment ('max_slot_wal_keep_size', '256MB') extracted from "max_wal_size sets the maximum amount of Write-Ahead-Logging (WAL) to grow between automatic checkpoints. This is a soft limit; WAL size can exceed max_wal_size under special circumstances, such as heavy load, a failing archive_command, or a high wal_keep_segments setting.
It should also be noted that increasing this parameter can increase the amount of time needed for crash recovery. The default value is 1GB (1024MB). max_slot_wal_keep_size "
